  {
    "id": "PE-P04",
    "title": "Banawali: a composite defence plan",
    "subtitle": "The legend distinguishes Pre-Harappan and Harappan defences",
    "source_id": "PE-S03",
    "locator": "Dholavira and Banawali: Two different paradigms of the Harappan Urbis forma (1999), p. 33, Figure 1; PDF index 46",
    "pdf_zero_based_index": 46,
    "printed_page": 33,
    "figure": "1",
    "phase": "Several periods in one published panel",
    "measurement_ids": [
      "PE-M008"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "B1 angle was withdrawn after the overlay showed an endpoint above the defence band. The mapped corner curves, so a unique straight intersection is absent.",
      "Bisht describes retaining and widening earlier defences while replacing domestic layouts in Period IC, then accepting the town outline with marginal changes in II (pp. 16-17).",
      "Those source-ordered events have no separate registered plan pair here. We cannot calculate how many internal walls or routes persisted.",
      "The 1983-84, 1987-88 and 1999 versions record publication and exposure changes. They are not earlier/later archaeological panels."
    ],
